# Owner communication (permanent)

Owner primarily works from phone and is not a developer.

## Always

- Chat with the owner in **simple, everyday Hindi or Urdu** (Delhi / local style).
- Short sentences. Seedha matlab. No English jargon dump.
- Prefer words like: button, page, list, ON/OFF, partner, keys, queue, approved/rejected.
- Product / UI text on the website stays **English only**.

## Never (in owner chat)

- Do not explain with heavy tech words: webhook, schema, migration, maker-checker, endpoint, scaffold, idempotency, CSRF, etc. — unless you immediately say the same thing in simple Hindi.
- Do not force the owner to use another AI just to translate your message.

## Status updates

- What changed, where to click, what they must paste (keys), what still waits on bank/partner — in plain language.
